# URLs that are live in a browser but return 403/anti-scrape to automated
# checkers (CDN/WAF bot-blocks). Add a line (regex) only after confirming the
# link is genuinely live in a browser. Keep this list short — every entry is a
# hole in the freshness guarantee. Re-verify during the quarterly sweep.

# US DoD WAF blocks all non-browser clients (canonical DoDAF page)
https://dodcio\.defense\.gov/library/dod-architecture-framework/
# TriMech training pages — Cloudflare bot challenge
https://enterprise\.trimech\.com/training-course/intro-to-mbse-and-sysml-with-cameo/
https://trimech\.com/intro-to-mbse-and-sysml-v2-training-course/
# Wiley / INCOSE Online Library — 403 to bots, live for readers
https://incose\.onlinelibrary\.wiley\.com/
# INCOSE main site (SE Handbook) — 403 to bots, live in a browser
https://www\.incose\.org/
# ResearchGate — blocks automated access
https://www\.researchgate\.net/
# GitHub issue-form link: written as the conventional relative ../../issues/new/choose
# (correct for browsers); lychee resolves it to a nonexistent local file path.
issues/new/choose
